<title>UK: UK Labour's Brown -will keep options open on EMU.</title>
<headline>UK Labour's Brown -will keep options open on EMU.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gordon Brown, the opposition Labour party's economics spokesman, said Labour would keep its options open in its policy on European monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;The decision will be taken in the national interest,&quot; Brown said in an interview on Reuters Financial Television when asked about policy on Europe. &quot;We will keep our options open.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 6784</p>
</text>
